  "notes": [
    "Credit sum: General Education 36 (Languages 9, Humanities 9, Social Sciences 6, Sciences 12) + School Core 21 + Math Requirements 6 + Major Requirements 18 + Economics Electives 12 + Free Electives 27 = 120.",
    "Courses marked * in the General Education and Major sections (BUS251, ECO101, ECO134, ECO172, MIS105) are counted only once, under School Core, as the document says.",
    "Sciences: 'three courses from BIO103/CHE101/ENV107/PBH101/PHY107/PSY101 with one credit lab each' (12 Cr) are three 4-credit slots that each list the other five options. Prerequisites printed as 'Check relevant department', so null.",
    "Social Sciences option 'ENV 203/GEO205' is listed as two alternatives with the same title.",
    "Economics Electives: 12 credits = 4 courses chosen from the 10 listed (ECO317 ... ECO492); modelled as 4 slots each listing the other nine. Each slot's prereq is that of its own code; the alternatives' prerequisites are not modelled. The document does not say whether other ECO courses also count.",
    "Free Electives 27 Cr = 12 Cr optional minor + 15 Cr from any area university-wide; modelled as 9 free elective placeholders of 3 credits.",
    "Prerequisites follow the curriculum table. Where the course descriptions on pages 3-5 differ, the table was kept: ECO173 table '-' but description 'ECO172' (description used, since the table gives none); ECO204 description adds ECO101; ECO328 description adds ECO201; ECO349 table ECO328 vs description ECO101, ECO104 (description used, because ECO328 is an alternative of the same slot); ECO354 description adds ECO204; ECO406 description ECO201, ECO204; ECO414 description adds ECO101; ECO372 description 'ECO173, MAT250' vs table 'ECO173/BUS173 & ECO134/BUS135/MAT120'; ECO201 description omits the BUS135/MAT120 options.",
    "ECO490 prerequisite '12 credits of ECO courses & ECO372' is stored as ECO372 only; the 12 ECO-credit condition cannot be expressed (a credits leaf counts all degree credits).",
    "ENG102 is added as a non-credit row (0 credits, not counted in the 120) because the document requires it for ENG103 'if not waived'; students with a waiver skip it.",
    "Prerequisite options dropped because those courses are not part of the Economics degree: BUS135 and MAT120 (printed as alternatives to ECO134 in 'ECO134/BUS135/MAT120' for ECO201, ECO204, ECO244, ECO301, ECO304, ECO372), so those rules now require ECO134; BUS173 (printed 'ECO173/BUS173' for ECO372), so ECO372 requires ECO173; MAT116 (printed prerequisite of MAT125), so MAT125 has no prerequisite.",
    "The document gives no semester plan, so semester is null. Row order follows the document."
  ],
